IMPORT prelude

-- Prevention of Corruption Act 1960 (Singapore) -- what a gratification and an agent are (s 2), the offences a person most meets
-- (ss 5, 6, 11, with the s 8 presumption and s 9), the most a conviction can cost (ss 5 to 7, 10 to 12, 18(2), 21(2), 26, 28, 32(2),
-- 29 to 31), the penalty on top for an accepted gratification (s 13), what a principal can recover (s 14), the evidence rules that
-- bear on the accused (ss 23, 24), arrest and search (s 15), the Public Prosecutor's notice (s 21), the public officer's duty to arrest
-- a briber (s 32(2)), consent to prosecute (s 33), indemnity (s 35), informers (s 36) and citizens abroad (s 37).
--
-- SEAT: the accused person -- an individual whose dealings with a gratification (as giver, receiver, agent, public servant or
-- tenderer) are in question, or who is served with a notice or arrested under the Act. Every decision is phrased as that person
-- would ask it.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to and including 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021),
-- current version as at 01 Oct 2026 on SSO, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PCA1960.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Part 2 (ss 3 to 4F: appointment of the Director and officers, the Occupational Superannuation Scheme): machinery. s 15A
-- (arms), s 16 (bail: a discretion handed to the Code), ss 17, 19 (investigation powers under the Criminal Procedure Code), s 18(1)
-- and s 20 (the Public Prosecutor's investigation and bank-book orders), s 22 (search warrants), s 25 (accomplice credit), s 26 and
-- s 28 elements (their punishment is encoded), s 27 (the duty to give information), s 34 (District Court jurisdiction), s 35(2) and
-- s 36(1), (2). The elements of ss 10 and 12 (their punishment is encoded). "Corruptly" is not defined by the Act: it is asked as the
-- court's finding. "Abets" and "criminal conspiracy" are the Penal Code's: asked as facts. The Act lays prohibitions; its one duty
-- with a deadline (s 21(2)) is written as a regulative rule.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Prevention of Corruption Act 1960 -- offences and what they cost`

§§ `2 -- gratification`

-- s 2: "gratification" includes -- "(a) money or any gift, loan, fee, reward, commission, valuable security or other property or
-- interest in property of any description"; "(b) any office, employment or contract"; "(c) any payment, release, discharge or
-- liquidation of any loan, obligation or other liability"; "(d) any other service, favour or advantage of any description whatsoever,
-- including protection from any penalty or disability ... or from any action or proceedings of a disciplinary or penal nature ... and
-- including the exercise or the forbearance from the exercise of any right or any official power or duty"; "(e) any offer, undertaking
-- or promise of any gratification within the meaning of paragraphs (a), (b), (c) and (d)".
-- Gloss: almost anything of value, including a favour, a job, a cancelled debt, or a mere promise of one.
-- The definition says "includes", so it is not closed. A thing it does not list is not decided here: NOTHING.
DECLARE Thing IS ONE OF
    `money`
    `a gift, loan, fee, reward or commission`
    `property or an interest in property`
    `an office, employment or contract`
    `the payment or release of a loan or other liability`
    `a service, favour or advantage`
    `protection from a penalty or from disciplinary or penal action`
    `an official using, or not using, a right, power or duty`
    `an offer, undertaking or promise of any of these`
    `something section 2 does not list`

GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a gratification` `the thing` IS
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `something section 2 does not list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `2 -- agent`

-- s 2: "agent" means "any person employed by or acting for another, and includes a trustee, administrator and executor, and a person
-- serving the Government or under any corporation or public body, and for the purposes of section 8 includes a subcontractor and any
-- person employed by or acting for such subcontractor".
-- Gloss: an employee, a trustee or executor, a civil servant, or anyone acting for someone else; a subcontractor only under s 8.
GIVEN `I am employed by, or act for, another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a trustee, administrator or executor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I serve the Government, or under a corporation or public body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a subcontractor, or employed by or acting for one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is asked for section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an agent` IF
        `I am employed by, or act for, another person`
    OR  `I am a trustee, administrator or executor`
    OR  `I serve the Government, or under a corporation or public body`
    OR  (`I am a subcontractor, or employed by or acting for one` AND `the question is asked for section 8`)

§§ `5, 6(a), 6(b), 8, 9 -- the corruption offences`

-- Which side of the gratification I was on. s 5(a): "corruptly solicit or receive, or agree to receive"; s 6(a): an agent "corruptly
-- accepts or obtains, or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain". s 5(b): "corruptly give, promise or offer"; s 6(b): "corruptly gives
-- or agrees to give or offers". Treating soliciting as an attempt to obtain, and promising as agreeing to give, is an INFERENCE.
DECLARE Side IS ONE OF
    `I solicited, received or agreed to receive it`
    `I gave, promised or offered it`

-- The facts of one dealing. "Corruptly" is not defined by the Act: whether I acted corruptly is the court's finding, an input.
-- s 8: "Where in any proceedings against a person for an offence under section 5 or 6, it is proved that any gratification has been
-- paid or given to or received by a person in the employment of the Government or any department thereof or of a public body by or
-- from a person or agent of a person who has or seeks to have any dealing with the Government or any department thereof or any public
-- body, that gratification shall be deemed to have been paid or given and received corruptly as an inducement or reward as
-- hereinbefore mentioned unless the contrary is proved."
-- Gloss: if a government or public-body employee actually got something from someone dealing with that body, the law assumes it was a
-- bribe unless I prove otherwise. Reading "as an inducement or reward as hereinbefore mentioned" as supplying the purpose limb of
-- ss 5 and 6 as well as "corruptly" is an INFERENCE. An offer or promise not yet paid, given or received does not raise it.
-- s 9(1), (2): an agent who accepted "having reason to believe or suspect" it was offered for an act or favour in relation to the
-- principal's affairs, or a giver who had reason to believe or suspect the agent had the power and the act was in relation to the
-- principal's affairs, is guilty "notwithstanding" that the agent had no power, right or opportunity, did not intend to, did not in
-- fact do so, or that the act was not in relation to the principal's affairs. The last two fields below are therefore never read.
DECLARE `My dealing` HAS
    `my side` IS A Side
    `what was involved` IS A Thing
    `the person on the receiving side is an agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was for someone doing or not doing something in a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was for an act or favour in relation to the agent's principal's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had reason to believe or suspect it concerned the principal's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds I acted corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the receiver was employed by the Government, a department or a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the giver, or the one they acted for, has or seeks dealings with the Government, a department or a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was actually paid, given or received` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied I proved the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent had no power or opportunity to do it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was never done` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Is it made out` IS ONE OF
    `yes, the elements are made out`
    `no, an element is missing`
    `not covered by this encoding: section 2 does not list the thing`

GIVEN d IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is corruption presumed against me under section 8` d IF
        d's `the receiver was employed by the Government, a department or a public body`
    AND d's `the giver, or the one they acted for, has or seeks dealings with the Government, a department or a public body`
    AND d's `it was actually paid, given or received`

GIVEN d IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the presumption stands against me` d IF
    `Is corruption presumed against me under section 8` d AND (NOT d's `the court is satisfied I proved the contrary`)

-- The other elements are checked first; only if they hold does an unlisted thing make the answer "not covered".
GIVEN `the other elements hold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A `Is it made out`
DECIDE `the verdict on` `the other elements hold` `the thing` IS
    IF NOT `the other elements hold`
    THEN `no, an element is missing`
    ELSE CONSIDER `Is it a gratification` `the thing`
         WHEN JUST g THEN IF g THEN `yes, the elements are made out` ELSE `no, an element is missing`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered by this encoding: section 2 does not list the thing`

-- s 5: either side, "for himself, or for any other person", "as an inducement to or reward for, or otherwise on account of -- (i) any
-- person doing or forbearing to do anything in respect of any matter or transaction whatsoever, actual or proposed; or (ii) any member,
-- officer or servant of a public body doing or forbearing" in a matter in which the body is concerned. (ii) falls within (i).
-- $100,000 or 5 years or both.
GIVEN d IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A `Is it made out`
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 5 offence` d IS
    `the verdict on`
        (    (d's `the court finds I acted corruptly` OR `the presumption stands against me` d)
         AND (d's `it was for someone doing or not doing something in a matter` OR `the presumption stands against me` d))
        (d's `what was involved`)

-- s 6(a): "any agent corruptly accepts or obtains, or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain, from any person, for himself or for any
-- other person, any gratification as an inducement or reward for doing or forbearing to do ... any act in relation to his principal's
-- affairs or business, or for showing or forbearing to show favour or disfavour to any person in relation to" them.
GIVEN d IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A `Is it made out`
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 6(a) offence` d IS
    `the verdict on`
        (    `I was the receiver` d
         AND d's `the person on the receiving side is an agent`
         AND (d's `the court finds I acted corruptly` OR `the presumption stands against me` d)
         AND (   d's `it was for an act or favour in relation to the agent's principal's affairs`
              OR d's `I had reason to believe or suspect it concerned the principal's affairs`
              OR `the presumption stands against me` d))
        (d's `what was involved`)

-- s 6(b): "any person corruptly gives or agrees to give or offers any gratification to any agent as an inducement or reward for doing
-- or forbearing to do ... any act in relation to his principal's affairs or business, or for showing or forbearing to show favour or
-- disfavour". s 9(2) saves the conviction where I had reason to believe or suspect the agent could act and it was the principal's affairs.
GIVEN d IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A `Is it made out`
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 6(b) offence` d IS
    `the verdict on`
        (    (NOT `I was the receiver` d)
         AND d's `the person on the receiving side is an agent`
         AND (d's `the court finds I acted corruptly` OR `the presumption stands against me` d)
         AND (   d's `it was for an act or favour in relation to the agent's principal's affairs`
              OR d's `I had reason to believe or suspect it concerned the principal's affairs`
              OR `the presumption stands against me` d))
        (d's `what was involved`)

GIVEN d IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I was the receiver` d IF
    CONSIDER d's `my side`
    WHEN `I solicited, received or agreed to receive it` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6(c) -- false documents and agents`

-- s 6(c): "any person knowingly gives to an agent, or if an agent knowingly uses with intent to deceive his principal, any receipt,
-- account or other document in respect of which the principal is interested, and which contains any statement which is false or
-- erroneous or defective in any material particular, and which to his knowledge is intended to mislead the principal".
-- Gloss: a false invoice or receipt handed to, or used by, someone's employee to fool the employer. No gratification and no
-- "corruptly" is needed.
GIVEN `I knowingly gave the document to an agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am an agent and knowingly used it intending to deceive my principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal is interested in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is false, erroneous or defective in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I knew it was meant to mislead the principal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 6(c) offence` IF
        (`I knowingly gave the document to an agent` OR `I am an agent and knowingly used it intending to deceive my principal`)
    AND `the principal is interested in the document`
    AND `it is false, erroneous or defective in a material particular`
    AND `I knew it was meant to mislead the principal`

§§ `11 -- Members of Parliament`

-- s 11: "(a) who offers any gratification to a Member of Parliament as an inducement or reward for such Member's doing or forbearing to
-- do any act in his capacity as such Member; or (b) who being a Member of Parliament solicits or accepts any gratification" for that.
-- $100,000 or 7 years or both. The section does not say "corruptly"; ss 10 and 12 do not either. The last input is never read.
GIVEN `I offered a gratification to a Member of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a Member of Parliament and solicited or accepted a gratification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was for an act or forbearance in the Member's capacity as a Member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court finds I acted corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 11 offence` IF
        (`I offered a gratification to a Member of Parliament` OR `I am a Member of Parliament and solicited or accepted a gratification`)
    AND `it was for an act or forbearance in the Member's capacity as a Member`

§§ `5 to 7, 10 to 12, 18(2), 21(2), 26, 28, 29 to 32 -- the most a conviction can cost`

-- The offence, as the person would name the charge.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `section 5(a) corruptly soliciting or receiving`
    `section 5(b) corruptly giving, promising or offering`
    `section 6(a) an agent corruptly accepting or obtaining`
    `section 6(b) corruptly giving or offering to an agent`
    `section 6(c) a false document given to or used by an agent`
    `section 10(a) offering for the withdrawal of a tender`
    `section 10(b) taking for withdrawing my tender`
    `section 11(a) offering to a Member of Parliament`
    `section 11(b) a Member of Parliament soliciting or accepting`
    `section 12(a) offering to a member of a public body`
    `section 12(b) a member of a public body soliciting or accepting`
    `section 18(2) failing to disclose or produce under an investigation order`
    `section 21(2) failing to comply with the Public Prosecutor's notice`
    `section 26 obstructing a search or investigation`
    `section 28 giving false or misleading information`
    `section 32(2) a public officer failing to arrest a briber`

-- ss 29 to 31: whoever abets (within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871), attempts, or is party to a criminal conspiracy to commit an
-- offence under this Act "shall be deemed to have committed the offence and shall be liable on conviction to be punished with the
-- punishment provided for that offence". So the part I played does not change the ceiling.
DECLARE Part IS ONE OF
    `I committed it myself`
    `I abetted it`
    `I attempted it`
    `I was party to a criminal conspiracy to commit it`

-- s 7: a person convicted under s 5 or 6 "where the matter or transaction in relation to which the offence was committed was a contract
-- or a proposal for a contract with the Government or any department thereof or with any public body or a subcontract to execute any
-- work comprised in such a contract" -- $100,000 or 7 years. Only the prison ceiling moves.
DECLARE `My sentencing facts` HAS
    `the offence I am convicted of` IS AN Offence
    `my part` IS A Part
    `the matter was a government or public-body contract, a proposal for one, or a subcontract under one` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Every figure is a maximum, "or ... or to both". The Act prints no minimum.
DECLARE `The most I face` IS ONE OF
    `a fine, prison, or both`
        HAS `fine up to` IS A NUMBER
            `months of prison up to` IS A NUMBER

-- ss 5, 6: $100,000 / 5 years (60 months); s 7: 7 years (84). ss 10, 11, 12: $100,000 / 7 years. s 18(2): $2,000 / one year.
-- s 21(2), s 26, s 28: $10,000 / one year. s 32(2): $5,000 / 6 months.
GIVEN f IS A `My sentencing facts`
GIVETH A `The most I face`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be punished with` f IS
    CONSIDER f's `the offence I am convicted of`
    WHEN `section 5(a) corruptly soliciting or receiving`                               THEN `sections 5 and 6, raised by section 7`
    WHEN `section 5(b) corruptly giving, promising or offering`                         THEN `sections 5 and 6, raised by section 7`
    WHEN `section 6(a) an agent corruptly accepting or obtaining`                       THEN `sections 5 and 6, raised by section 7`
    WHEN `section 6(b) corruptly giving or offering to an agent`                        THEN `sections 5 and 6, raised by section 7`
    WHEN `section 6(c) a false document given to or used by an agent`                   THEN `sections 5 and 6, raised by section 7`
    WHEN `section 18(2) failing to disclose or produce under an investigation order`    THEN `a fine, prison, or both`   2000 12
    WHEN `section 21(2) failing to comply with the Public Prosecutor's notice`          THEN `a fine, prison, or both`  10000 12
    WHEN `section 26 obstructing a search or investigation`                             THEN `a fine, prison, or both`  10000 12
    WHEN `section 28 giving false or misleading information`                            THEN `a fine, prison, or both`  10000 12
    WHEN `section 32(2) a public officer failing to arrest a briber`                    THEN `a fine, prison, or both`   5000  6
    OTHERWISE                                                                                `a fine, prison, or both` 100000 84
    WHERE
        `sections 5 and 6, raised by section 7` MEANS
            IF f's `the matter was a government or public-body contract, a proposal for one, or a subcontract under one`
            THEN `a fine, prison, or both` 100000 84
            ELSE `a fine, prison, or both` 100000 60

§§ `13 -- the penalty on top for an accepted gratification`

-- s 13(1): where a court convicts a person "of an offence committed by the acceptance of any gratification", then "if that
-- gratification is a sum of money or if the value of that gratification can be assessed, the court shall, in addition to imposing on
-- that person any other punishment, order him to pay as a penalty ... a sum which is equal to the amount of that gratification or is,
-- in the opinion of the court, the value of that gratification", recoverable as a fine. (2): where other outstanding offences of
-- acceptance are taken into consideration under s 148 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, the court "may increase the penalty ... by
-- an amount not exceeding the total amount or value of the gratification specified in the charges for the offences so taken into
-- consideration".
-- Gloss: if I am convicted of taking a bribe, I must pay back its value on top of my sentence, and more for charges taken into account.
DECLARE `My acceptance` HAS
    `I am convicted of an offence committed by accepting a gratification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is money, or its value can be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its amount, or its value in the court's opinion` IS A NUMBER
    `the total in the charges taken into consideration` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `The section 13 penalty` IS ONE OF
    `no section 13 penalty`
    `a penalty on top of my sentence`
        HAS `the court must order` IS A NUMBER
            `and may raise it to at most` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN a IS A `My acceptance`
GIVETH A `The section 13 penalty`
DECIDE `What penalty must I pay on top of my sentence` a IS
    IF a's `I am convicted of an offence committed by accepting a gratification` AND a's `it is money, or its value can be assessed`
    THEN `a penalty on top of my sentence`
            (a's `its amount, or its value in the court's opinion`)
            (a's `its amount, or its value in the court's opinion` PLUS a's `the total in the charges taken into consideration`)
    ELSE `no section 13 penalty`

§§ `14 -- what my principal can recover`

-- s 14(1): "Where any gratification has, in contravention of this Act, been given by any person to an agent, the principal may recover
-- as a civil debt the amount or the money value thereof either from the agent or from the person who gave the gratification to the
-- agent, and no conviction or acquittal of the defendant in respect of an offence under this Act shall operate as a bar". The last
-- input is therefore never read.
GIVEN `a gratification was given to an agent in contravention of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am that agent or the person who gave it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its amount or money value` IS A NUMBER
      `I was acquitted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can the principal recover from me as a civil debt` IS
    IF `a gratification was given to an agent in contravention of this Act` AND `I am that agent or the person who gave it`
    THEN `its amount or money value`
    ELSE 0

§§ `23, 24 -- evidence against me`

-- s 23: "In any civil or criminal proceeding under this Act evidence shall not be admissible to show that any such gratification as is
-- mentioned in this Act is customary in any profession, trade, vocation or calling." Outside such a proceeding the Act says nothing.
GIVEN `the proceeding is a civil or criminal proceeding under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my evidence that such gifts are customary in my trade shut out` IF
    `the proceeding is a civil or criminal proceeding under this Act`

-- s 24(1): in a trial for an offence under this Act or Penal Code ss 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 (or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment),
-- that the accused possesses, "for which he cannot satisfactorily account, ... pecuniary resources or property disproportionate to his
-- known sources of income", or obtained an unexplained accretion "at or about the time of the alleged offence", "may be proved and may
-- be taken into consideration by the court as corroborating the testimony of any witness" that the accused took a gratification, and
-- as showing it was taken corruptly. (2): resources held by another whom there is reason to believe holds them in trust for or on
-- behalf of the accused, or as a gift from the accused, are deemed the accused's.
-- Gloss: unexplained wealth can back up a witness who says I took a bribe. Whether I account for it satisfactorily is the court's view.
GIVEN `the trial is for a corruption offence under this Act or Penal Code ss 161 to 165 or 213 to 215` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I hold resources or property out of proportion to my known income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone else holds such resources for me in trust, on my behalf, or as my gift` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gained an accretion to my resources at about the time of the alleged offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court finds I can satisfactorily account for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my unexplained wealth corroborate the case against me` IF
        `the trial is for a corruption offence under this Act or Penal Code ss 161 to 165 or 213 to 215`
    AND (   `I hold resources or property out of proportion to my known income`
         OR `someone else holds such resources for me in trust, on my behalf, or as my gift`
         OR `I gained an accretion to my resources at about the time of the alleged offence`)
    AND (NOT `the court finds I can satisfactorily account for it`)

§§ `15 -- arrest and search`

-- s 15(1): "The Director or any special investigator may without a warrant arrest any person who has been concerned in any offence under
-- this Act or against whom a reasonable complaint has been made or credible information has been received or a reasonable suspicion
-- exists of his having been so concerned." (3): the person arrested "shall be taken to the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau or to
-- a police station". Gloss: the Director and special investigators are officers of the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau.
-- Whether a complaint is reasonable or a suspicion exists is the officer's judgment, asked as such.
GIVEN `the officer is the Director or a special investigator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have been concerned in an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable complaint has been made, credible information received, or a reasonable suspicion exists that I was` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can this officer arrest me without a warrant` IF
        `the officer is the Director or a special investigator`
    AND (   `I have been concerned in an offence under this Act`
         OR `a reasonable complaint has been made, credible information received, or a reasonable suspicion exists that I was`)

-- s 15(2): the arresting Director or special investigator "may search such person and take possession of all articles found upon him
-- which there is reason to believe were the fruits or other evidence of the crime, provided that no female shall be searched except by
-- a female".
GIVEN `I was arrested under section 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am female` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer who would search me is female` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the officer search me` IF
        `I was arrested under section 15(1)`
    AND ((NOT `I am female`) OR `the officer who would search me is female`)

§§ `21 -- the Public Prosecutor's notice`

-- s 21(1): in an investigation or proceedings into an offence "by any person in the service of the Government or of any department
-- thereof or of any public body" under this Act or Penal Code ss 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 (or conspiracy, attempt, abetment), the
-- Public Prosecutor may by written notice "(a) require that person to furnish a sworn statement in writing enumerating all movable or
-- immovable property belonging to or possessed by that person and by the spouse, sons and daughters of that person, and specifying the
-- date on which each of the properties enumerated was acquired"; ... "(c) require any other person to furnish a sworn statement in
-- writing enumerating all movable or immovable property belonging to or possessed by that person where the Public Prosecutor has
-- reasonable grounds to believe that the information can assist the investigation".
DECLARE `What I can be made to declare` IS ONE OF
    `my property and my spouse's and children's, with the dates each was acquired`
    `my own property`
    `nothing under section 21(1)(a) or (c)`

GIVEN `I am in the service of the Government, a department or a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investigation is into a corruption offence by me under this Act or Penal Code ss 161 to 165 or 213 to 215` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Public Prosecutor has reasonable grounds to believe my information can assist the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What I can be made to declare`
DECIDE `What can the Public Prosecutor make me declare on oath` IS
    BRANCH
        IF      `I am in the service of the Government, a department or a public body`
            AND `the investigation is into a corruption offence by me under this Act or Penal Code ss 161 to 165 or 213 to 215`
            THEN `my property and my spouse's and children's, with the dates each was acquired`
        IF `the Public Prosecutor has reasonable grounds to believe my information can assist the investigation`
            THEN `my own property`
        OTHERWISE `nothing under section 21(1)(a) or (c)`

-- s 21(2): "Every person to whom a notice is sent by the Public Prosecutor under subsection (1) shall, notwithstanding the provisions of
-- any written law or any oath of secrecy to the contrary, comply with the terms of that notice within such time as may be specified
-- therein and any person who wilfully neglects or fails so to comply shall be guilty of an offence" -- $10,000 or one year or both.
-- The duty, with its deadline:
DECLARE `Person served` IS ONE OF `me, the person served with the notice`
DECLARE `What the notice requires` IS ONE OF `comply with the terms of the notice`

GIVEN `the days the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person served` `What the notice requires`
DECIDE `my duty to comply with the Public Prosecutor's notice` IS
    PARTY `me, the person served with the notice`
    MUST  `comply with the terms of the notice`
    WITHIN `the days the notice allows`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `me, the person served with the notice`

-- The offence. An oath of secrecy or another written law is no answer, so the last input is never read.
GIVEN `a notice under section 21(1) was sent to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I complied within the time it specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my failure was wilful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an oath of secrecy or another written law forbids me to disclose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 21(2) offence` IF
        `a notice under section 21(1) was sent to me`
    AND (NOT `I complied within the time it specified`)
    AND `my failure was wilful`

§§ `32(2) -- a public officer offered a bribe`

-- s 32(2): "A public officer to whom any gratification is corruptly given or offered shall arrest the person who gives or offers the
-- gratification to him and make over the person so arrested to the nearest police station and if he fails to do so without reasonable
-- excuse he shall be guilty of an offence" -- $5,000 or 6 months or both. No deadline is stated.
GIVEN `I am a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a gratification was corruptly given or offered to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I arrested the giver and handed them over at the nearest police station` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 32(2) offence` IF
        `I am a public officer`
    AND `a gratification was corruptly given or offered to me`
    AND (NOT `I arrested the giver and handed them over at the nearest police station`)
    AND (NOT `I had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `33, 35, 36, 37 -- prosecution, indemnity, informers, acts abroad`

-- s 33: "A prosecution under this Act shall not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor brought, or consented to, the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a prosecution under this Act be instituted against me` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor brought, or consented to, the prosecution`

-- s 35(1): where 2 or more persons are charged, "the court may require one or more of them to give evidence as a witness or witnesses
-- for the prosecution". (3): every person so required who "in the opinion of the court makes true and full discovery of all things as
-- to which he is lawfully examined, shall be entitled to receive a certificate of indemnity", which "shall be a bar to all legal
-- proceedings against him in respect of all those things".
GIVEN `I am one of 2 or more persons charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court required me to give evidence for the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion I made true and full discovery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a certificate of indemnity` IF
        `I am one of 2 or more persons charged`
    AND `the court required me to give evidence for the prosecution`
    AND `the court is of the opinion I made true and full discovery`

-- s 36(1): no witness "shall be obliged or permitted to disclose the name or address of any informer". (3): "If on a trial for any
-- offence under this Act the court, after full inquiry into the case, is of the opinion that the informer wilfully made in his complaint
-- a material statement which he knew or believed to be false or did not believe to be true, or if in any other proceeding the court is
-- of the opinion that justice cannot be fully done between the parties thereto without the discovery of the informer, the court may ...
-- permit inquiry and require full disclosure concerning the informer." Even then it is the court's choice ("may").
GIVEN `I am on trial for an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks the informer wilfully made a material statement they knew or believed false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks justice cannot be done in this other proceeding without discovering the informer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court open up who informed against me` IF
    IF `I am on trial for an offence under this Act`
    THEN `the court thinks the informer wilfully made a material statement they knew or believed false`
    ELSE `the court thinks justice cannot be done in this other proceeding without discovering the informer`

-- s 37(1): "The provisions of this Act have effect, in relation to citizens of Singapore, outside as well as within Singapore; and where
-- an offence under this Act is committed by a citizen of Singapore in any place outside Singapore, he may be dealt with in respect of
-- that offence as if it had been committed within Singapore." For a non-citizen abroad, s 37 is silent (s 29(b) reaches abetment in
-- Singapore of acts abroad for a principal residing in Singapore; not encoded).
DECLARE `Acts abroad` IS ONE OF
    `the act was in Singapore; section 37 is not needed`
    `yes, I can be dealt with as if it were done in Singapore`
    `not covered by this encoding: section 37 reaches only citizens`

GIVEN `the act was done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Acts abroad`
DECIDE `Can I be dealt with here for what I did abroad` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act was done outside Singapore` THEN `the act was in Singapore; section 37 is not needed`
        IF `I am a citizen of Singapore` THEN `yes, I can be dealt with as if it were done in Singapore`
        OTHERWISE `not covered by this encoding: section 37 reaches only citizens`
